{
  "case_id": "2009-09-60",
  "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument first this morning in Case 09-60, Carachuri-Rosendo v. Holder. Mr. Srinivasan."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Srinivasan (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Long-time lawful permanent resident aliens with two convictions for minor drug possession offenses are subject to removal from the United States, but they are not categorically ineligible to seek discretionary relief from removal from the Attorney General based on their connections and deep family ties to the country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Ginsburg: Mr. Srinivasan, as a threshold question, is there a mootness problem here, because, as I understand it, the Petitioner came back to the country illegally and committed another minor crime?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Srinivasan (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SRINIVASAN: That's not correct, Justice Ginsburg, in our view. And the government, it's notable, doesn't make a mootness argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I don't know. It seems to me you go further than you need to and, moreover, imagine a State offense that just says possession of marijuana, zero to 5 years."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Saharsky",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SAHARSKY: A two-step inquiry. There are two questions. The first is: Does the State offense correspond to an offense under the CSA? Does it correspond to a Federal offense, and that\u2019s based on the elements, and the Court said that that was based on the elements on page 51 of Nijhawan --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Ms. Saharsky, do we take into account at all -- I mean, in Lopez as I understand it, the petitioner prevailed because it would not have been a felony under the Federal law. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. SAHARSKY",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Immigration is very different from criminal proceedings. This Court has said that on numerous occasions the rights in terms of due process and counsel and the like are very different. And in immigration, Congress made a categorical judgment that individuals who have been convicted of conduct should all be treated the same and that they all should be removed from the United States and should be -- not be able to get discretionary relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. SAHARSKY",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you look all through the aggravated felony provisions -- they are in our brief; there are 21 of them -- for none of those provisions was Congress concerned about notice or the like."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Can I ask you a related question, which will show what I'm trying -- another thing that\u2019s worrying me. Suppose we\u2019re in the Armed Career Criminal Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. SAHARSKY",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0002-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress has made a judgment since 1970 in the drug laws that two drug possession offenses should be punishable as a felony."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: We usually think of recidivism when we talk about statistics as being repeated for any crime. This is a recidivism of a special kind. It's repeating the same -- the same thing. Is that essential to your argument? I know it's essential to the -- to the Federal statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Srinivasan)",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SRINIVASAN: Right, and because it's essential to the Federal statute, it's necessarily a part of our argument. I don't think our argument would be any different if the Federal statute read differently, but you can only be punishable as a felon under Federal law if you had a prior drug conviction, and if you had a prior drug conviction that was in fact found to exist."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0003-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you can only be punishable as a felon under Federal law if you had a prior drug conviction, and if you had a prior drug conviction that was in fact found to exist."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: How do you distinguish Nijhawan? I mean, there what made it a Federal felony was the fact that more than $10,000 was obtained from the victims. But that was not found in the -- in the State conviction. It simply was not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Srinivasan)",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdffce94a2fd-0003-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As a consequence, that person cannot as a matter of law receive a felony sentence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-09-60",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "cdffce94a2fd3d8362ddaac0418a95a422df16619c382d93b5cbb7427ae67845",
